    "problem_statement": "Secret deletion functionality broken after recent changes\n\n#### Description\n\nAfter a recent update, the secret deletion functionality in AWS Secrets Manager is not working properly. When trying to delete secrets, the operation appears to succeed but the secret's deletion state is not being tracked correctly.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport boto3\nfrom moto import mock_aws\n\n@mock_aws\ndef test_delete_secret_issue():\n    conn = boto3.client('secretsmanager', region_name='us-west-2')\n    \n    # Create a secret\n    conn.create_secret(Name='test-secret', SecretString='foosecret')\n    \n    # Delete the secret\n    deleted_secret = conn.delete_secret(SecretId='test-secret')\n    print(\"Delete response:\", deleted_secret)\n    \n    # Try to describe the secret - should show it's deleted\n    secret_details = conn.describe_secret(SecretId='test-secret')\n    print(\"Secret details:\", secret_details)\n    \n    # This should fail since secret is deleted\n    try:\n        conn.get_secret_value(SecretId='test-secret')\n        print(\"ERROR: Should not be able to get value of deleted secret!\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(\"Expected error:\", e)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    test_delete_secret_issue()\n```\n\nThe delete operation returns successfully but subsequent operations don't behave as if the secret is actually deleted. The secret should be marked with a deletion date and certain operations should fail when attempted on deleted secrets.\n\nAlso having issues with:\n- Creating secrets without values\n- Updating secrets without values  \n- Restoring deleted secrets\n- Various operations on deleted secrets not properly checking deletion status",
